  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-01-02T04:42:10.801Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Since we already have a button to bring up a menu hovering in mid-air, and we already have in-world web panels which display whatever web page we want, I thought it might be nice if we could combine the two, and have a web browser inside the menu.\n\nMy own use cases would be:\n\n* Seeing Twitter notifications when the phone makes a sound\n* Looking up stuff in dictionaries (I find myself having to translate obscure terms between languages more often than I would like lol)\n* Maybe checking up on whether forums have updates and other various out-world social networking type stuff\n\nMainly I'd like to avoid things which currently require removing the headset and putting on my glasses.\n\nBeing able to show it to other users might be nice sometimes too. Maybe you just want to show your Twitter ID to another person or something. (I see some people literally building this into their models' hand gestures.) I can totally see the potential for abuse here too, but we already have people running around with custom avatars, so how bad could it be?",
